Maybe next time..."}]}}]}, {"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [], "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0, "selected": 0}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "pdf", "content": "engenn8le15ob11re7pdf01.pdf"}]}]}], "type": "DWS", "id": 11, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " \nAsk to go to Space Camp!\n"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Take Away"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment.\n"}]}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}]}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn8le15ob11re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn8le15ob11re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn8le15ob11re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn8le15ob11re2img01.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "If your children dream of becoming astronauts, you will want to send them to space camp. It's the place that can make their dreams come true! If you can afford it, the five-day program in the U.S. will teach them all it takes to be an astronaut."}, {"time": "14000", "image": "engenn8le15ob11re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<p>They would get to experience what astronauts go through on a space mission. Simulators would be used so they could experience what it's like to be in the heavens.</p>\nIf they want to know how it feels to move under the moon's low gravitational pull, they can. If they want to know what it's like to float in a spacecraft that's orbiting Earth, here's where they can do that."}, {"time": "37000", "image": "engenn8le15ob11re2img02.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "<p>In the space camp, children learn about the procedures that are involved in space travel. If they are interested in making their own rockets, we'll help them. They also get to fit themselves into space suits to see how difficult it is to control their movements in them. They might even be persuaded to try freeze-dried space food! (Nothing genetically modified here!)</p>\nBy the end of the program, campers should be prepared for the final test - one hour at the helm of the a Space Shuttle simulator.\nDoes it sound like fun? Well, most NASA wannabes say that space camp \"is a real blast.\""}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Science, Old and New"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Space Camp"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 15}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "   Describe events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn8le15ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The First Conditional"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use the First Conditional to talk about real possibilities in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": " You use the First Conditional to say it's possible that you will do   something. In that condition, something else will happen."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span> clause\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Main Clause\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> If your children dream of becoming astronauts,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">  you will want to send them to space camp.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> If they want to know how it feels to move under the moon's low gravitational pull,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">they can.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": " If you can afford it, the five-day program in the U.S. will teach them all it takes to be an astronaut."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If they want to know how it feels to move under the moon's low gravitational pull, they can. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If they want to know what it's like to float in a spacecraft that's orbiting Earth, here's where they can do that."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If they are interested in making their own rockets, we'll help them."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Modal Verbs in the Passive Voice"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use modal verbs to add meaning to other verbs.  They come before the dictionary form (infinitive without <span class=\"italic\">to</span>) of the main verb. <br/>Modal verbs can add meaning connected with certainty or obligation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use modal verbs in the passive voice. <br/> You use the passive voice when you want to focus  on the \"receiver\" of the action, rather than the \"doer\" of the action. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The form of a passive sentence, with a modal, is:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Subject + modal + to be + past participle"}, {"type": "text", "content": "  For example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Simulators would be used </span>so they could experience what it's like to be in the heavens.  </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "They would get to experience what astronauts go through on a space mission. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Simulators would be used so they could experience what it's like to be in the heavens."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Space Camp is where they can do that."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They might even be persuaded to try freeze-dried space food."}, {"type": "example", "content": "By the end of the program, campers should be prepared for the final test."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "modified"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "changed in form or character"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: How many of the foods you eat are genetically modified?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le15ob11aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words to review."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to fit"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to be adapted to or suitable for (a purpose, object, occasion, etc.)"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They said he could be fitted with a robotic prosthesis."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le15ob11aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to control"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to dominate or command "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  The prosthesis could be controlled with his mind. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le15ob11aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "helm"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in charge of something or in the position of a leader"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: One hour at the helm of the a Space Shuttle simulator."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le15ob11aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "procedure"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a way of performing or effecting something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If they have the procedure, they may develop serious complications following it. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le15ob11aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "heavens"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the space that surrounds the earth"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  With their eyes on the heavens, men began to wonder whether the stars and planets they saw could be explored."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le15ob11aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "gravitational"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "connected or pulled together by a strong force"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The Earth's strong gravitational pull would have to be overcome before rockets could escape the stratosphere."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le15ob11aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to orbit"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to follow a circular path around another object like a sun or a planet"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The U.S. and the Soviet Union took turns sending satellites and men into orbit. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le15ob11aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "NASA"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an agency of the U.S.A. whose acronym means  National Aeronautics and Space Administration"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If you log onto the NASA website, you will see pictures and data sent back by dozens of space probes."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le15ob11aud09"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Imagine that you are 10 years old and interested in Space Camp."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a letter asking your parents if you can go."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Say what you'll do if you go there."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Say how you will feel if they allow it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain what you will be like for the rest of the year if they give you this opportunity."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your letter aloud to a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write a letter asking my parent if I can go to space camp."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use cause and effect clauses to say what I will do and feel."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I say how I will act if allowed to go."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my letter with a partner."}]}]}